y, I can focus on the suited tiles and try to form Pungs or Chows in the future.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing J1 (Red Dragon) is the optimal choice to discard an unnecessary honor tile, avoiding potential points for others while maintaining flexibility in forming suited tile melds.\nReason: Discarding J1 removes a single honor tile that doesn't contribute to current patterns and reduces the risk of others completing Dragon-related scoring. Keeping W4/W8 pairs preserves potential for Pung/Kong development. The B4-B5-B6 sequence is safer to retain than risk breaking it.\nAnswer: Play J1"}
